    st.markdown("""
    ### 🎯 Stage 4 Technical System Architecture
    > **"TrafficFlow AI is an explainable, calibrated spatiotemporal traffic early-warning engine. It fuses direct multi-horizon machine learning models (5 min, 10 min, 15 min) with Temporal Risk Momentum (TRM), Spatial Congestion Pressure (SCP), and Propagation Shock (PSI) to provide reliable advance signals before physical bottlenecks develop."**

    ---

    ### 🏭 Real-World Live-Data Deployment Architecture
    1. **Streaming Telemetry Ingestion:**
       - Direct highway loop detector feeds ingested over Apache Kafka / MQTT topics at 5-minute sampling windows.
       - End-to-end telemetry parsing, causal gap detection, and forward-fill clamping executed within <150 ms latency.
    2. **Graceful Sensor Dropout Handling:**
       - If a detector drops offline, the system falls back to causal historical medians and spatial neighbor consensus, preserving full network inference stability up to 30% outages.
    3. **Continuous Calibration & Drift Detection:**
       - Brier Score Loss and Expected Calibration Error (ECE) continuously tracked over rolling 7-day windows.
       - Statistical drift triggers automated alert recalibration without cold retraining.
    4. **Scientific Honesty Statement:**
       - All propagation links represent data-driven empirical lead-lag correlation tendencies and do not imply physical road topological certainty.
       - Directionally uncertain relationships are explicitly preserved as uncertain.
    """)
